  "a_point": "When an insured person receives a partial or full disability pension from a pension fund, the fund must split the pension assets into an active and a passive account under Art. 15 OPP 2 and continue to manage them under Art. 14 OPP 2; the insured cannot claim the payment in cash of the divorce-related free‑passage amount held in the fund’s passive account, because Art. 16 OLP only covers free‑passage accounts/policies that insure only the old‑age risk, not the assets already allocated to the disability pension.",
